msgid "JSON-LD"
msgstr ""

msgid "Override the title, description, share image, indexing and JSON-LD for individual static pages. Leave a field blank to fall back to the page’s own content and the site-wide defaults set in Configure. Resource (item) pages derive their SEO automatically and are not listed here."
msgstr ""

msgid "Access statement for research items"
msgstr ""

msgid "Closes the schema.org conditionsOfAccess of every research item (an item that is part of a project), after its recorded access rights. Leave blank for the default, translated into the page language: “AMIRA holds the description of this material, not the material itself. Requests for access go to the research project named in the record.”"
msgstr ""

msgid "AMIRA holds the description of this material, not the material itself. Requests for access go to the research project named in the record."
msgstr ""

msgid "Noindex filtered / paginated browse pages"
msgstr ""

msgid "Keeps faceted and paginated browse URLs, search results pages (Omeka’s site search and DRE Search) and any other URL with a query string out of the index — they add little and dilute crawl budget — while crawlers still follow their links to the resource pages. A record paging through its connection lists stays indexable. Recommended."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ping IndexNow when content changes"
msgstr ""

msgid "Notifies Bing/Yandex (and other IndexNow engines) when a public item, item set or page is added, edited, made private or deleted, so the change is crawled sooner. Concurrent edits are coalesced into one background batch; very large batches are left to the sitemap. Google is not pinged (its ping endpoint was retired — Google uses robots.txt + Search Console instead)."
msgstr ""
